<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet>
  <title>Homework 05: Content Moderation Fairness</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      <alert>Instructions:</alert> Answer the questions below using classification metrics and fairness reasoning.
      Think about how the mathematics informs real platform governance decisions.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <page>
    <exercise>
      <title>Confusion Matrix and Fairness</title>
      <statement>
        <p>
          A social platform uses an automated classifier to flag content for removal. The classifier is evaluated on two groups, X and Y.
        </p>
        <table>
          <title>Classifier Results</title>
          <tabular>
            <row><cell>Group</cell><cell>True Positive</cell><cell>False Positive</cell><cell>False Negative</cell><cell>True Negative</cell></row>
            <row><cell>X</cell><cell>50</cell><cell>25</cell><cell>30</cell><cell>195</cell></row>
            <row><cell>Y</cell><cell>40</cell><cell>10</cell><cell>20</cell><cell>230</cell></row>
          </tabular>
        </table>

        <ol>
          <li><p>Compute precision and recall for each group.</p></li>
          <li><p>Compare the false-positive and false-negative rates for the two groups. Which group is more likely to have acceptable content removed? Which group is more likely to have disallowed content remain?</p></li>
          <li><p>Explain why these differences matter for platform governance, especially for communities that are historically marginalized.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
  </page>

  <page>
    <exercise>
      <title>Policy Trade-Offs</title>
      <statement>
        <ol>
          <li><p>Suppose the platform can change the classification threshold to reduce false positives for Group X while increasing false negatives for both groups. What are the governance trade-offs involved in making that choice?</p></li>
          <li><p>Describe one fairness criterion the platform could adopt (for example, demographic parity or equal opportunity) and how it would change the decision rule.</p></li>
          <li><p>Choose a real platform policy (e.g. a social media community standard or a moderation guideline) and briefly analyze one way it could cause disparate impact.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </statement>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>
